-- CREATE OR MODIFY WORKFLOW and ALTER WORKFLOW over MCP scrambled the flow.
--
-- Symptom (mxcli exec --mcp …, Studio Pro 11.14; read back with ped_read_document):
--   * `create or modify` of a workflow stored its activities reversed, with an
--     activity of the old flow left in and one of the new ones missing:
--     [Start, a, b, End] rewritten as A, B, C came back Start, B, A, a, End;
--     a larger one also lost its parallel split and held a name twice;
--   * `alter workflow … replace activity X with …` changed nothing — X stayed;
--   * inserting several activities at once interleaved them with the ones after
--     the anchor (not reachable from MDL, whose INSERT AFTER takes one activity).
-- No error was reported by the update itself.
--
-- Cause: one ped_update_document batch does not apply its ops in the order sent.
-- Measured with raw PED calls: the ops run highest index first, and at one index
-- the adds go in as a block, in op order, before the removes — so a remove where
-- something was just added takes the added element. mxcli sent removes and adds
-- for the same list in one batch, and its adds in reverse or at incrementing
-- indices.
--
-- Fix (mdl/backend/mcp/workflow.go): a list's new elements go in at one index in
-- the statement's order, and the elements they replace are removed in a second
-- update — for the flow, the event sub-processes and the event handlers, and for
-- ALTER's replace.
--
-- Needs a project with module `workflow` and entity `workflow.workfow1context`
-- (ako/TestApp). Both statements run in one exec: the second sees the workflow the
-- first created, so it is an update.
--
-- Verify:
--   mxcli exec mdl-examples/bug-tests/mcp-workflow-update-order.mdl -p app.mpr --mcp <url>
--   ped_read_document /flow/activities on workflow.ZzMxcliBug_UpdateOrder
--   → Start, updA, updB, updInserted, updReplaced, End ; ped_check_errors → "No errors found."

create workflow workflow.ZzMxcliBug_UpdateOrder
  parameter $WorkflowContext: workflow.workfow1context
begin
  wait for notification oldA comment 'Old A';
  wait for notification oldB comment 'Old B';
end workflow;

create or modify workflow workflow.ZzMxcliBug_UpdateOrder
  parameter $WorkflowContext: workflow.workfow1context
begin
  wait for notification updA comment 'A';
  wait for notification updB comment 'B';
  wait for notification updC comment 'C';
end workflow;

alter workflow workflow.ZzMxcliBug_UpdateOrder
  insert after updB wait for notification updInserted comment 'Inserted after B';

alter workflow workflow.ZzMxcliBug_UpdateOrder
  replace activity updC with wait for notification updReplaced comment 'Replaced C';
